From bc5ba48345fe066e283ee96e2a7529ae6b63f1f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florent Merlet <florentmerlet73@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:57:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] TIP 759 (3/7): lists (a, b, ...) in expressions

In an expression, two or more expressions separated by commas, in
parentheses that do not follow a function name, give the list of their
values: expr {($x, $y)}, lmap a $L0 b $L1 {($a, $b)}.

- ParseExpr: a NULL_FUNC node is made before each open paren that is not
  a function's; a comma at the top of the parens turns it into a LIST
  node. NULL_FUNC does nothing and keeps constant folding.
- CompileExprTree: LIST compiles to INST_LIST; its value is not
  converted to a number.
- ConvertTreeToTokens (Tcl_ParseExpr): NULL_FUNC has no tokens; a list
  is shown as a call whose operator token is empty.
- Tests: exprList.test; parseExpr-21.32. Docs: expr.n.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MrNWAEyXLqekovNBvbMZ4z
